# Wave 4 Log

## Status

- Started: 2026-09-21
- Scope: project CRUD Route Handlers, full-save API, chart read API
- Status: Complete

## Implemented

- Added `app/lib/server/db/app-database.ts` to apply migrations when opening an application DB connection.
- Added project Route Handlers:
  - `GET /api/projects`
  - `POST /api/projects`
  - `GET /api/projects/:id`
  - `PUT /api/projects/:id`
  - `DELETE /api/projects/:id`
- Added `GET /api/projects/:id/chart`.
- Added route ID parsing and shared route error handling.
- Full save returns the latest project tree with newly assigned integer IDs.
- Chart responses add `displayName` using the shared chord realization engine.
- Routes work against a clean DB because migrations are applied on connection.

## Contract Decisions

- No section-level or chord-level mutation APIs are exposed.
- Client edits remain draft state and are persisted only through full project PUT.
- Project PUT validates the entire tree before starting the transaction.
- Project PUT response is the re-hydration snapshot for the client.
- Empty bars are returned with `chords: []`.

## Issues / Resolutions

### W4-001: Clean DB API startup

- Observation: Wave 3 repositories assumed migrations had already run, while a fresh Next.js process could receive project API requests before a CLI migration.
- Resolution: Project API connections now apply idempotent migrations before repository operations.
- Result: A clean temporary DB passed the full HTTP flow without a separate migration command.

### W4-002: Dynamic route parameters

- Observation: Next.js 15 App Router dynamic route parameters are asynchronous.
- Resolution: Route Handlers use `params: Promise<{ id: string }>` and await the context before parsing IDs.

